;
; xymonapi's SELinux module, in CIL, which semodule loads as it is: the
; install loads it where SELinux is active, and removes it with the plugin.
;
; The web server's snippets pass /xymon/api/ to the API's relay socket,
; $XYMONRUNDIR/xymonapi/relay.sock. The web server runs as httpd_t; the
; API, a task of xymonlaunch, as unconfined_service_t, and the socket takes
; its directory's label, httpd_sys_rw_content_t where Xymon's RPM labels
; /run/xymon. Every Xymon daemon runs as unconfined_service_t, so the rule
; cannot name the API alone: it lets httpd connect to the stream sockets
; of every unconfined daemon. Hence the boolean, off: the admin who wants
; the relay sets it, setsebool -P xymonapi_relay on (xymonapi(8)).
(boolean xymonapi_relay false)
(booleanif xymonapi_relay
    (true
        (allow httpd_t unconfined_service_t (unix_stream_socket (connectto)))
        (allow httpd_t httpd_sys_rw_content_t (sock_file (write)))))
